{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788980639,"nonce":"ySIRivpuk/RZwU1Yl5ccrHIfBjc=","message":"ArraySize and GetTID are guarded, following the null/load/cont diamond GetType already uses. ArraySize answers 0 and GetTID answers the register's static type kind, both matching the interpreter. A select was not usable: it evaluates both arms, and the load is what faults.\n\nA SECOND divergence in ArraySize, deliberately left alone because it is not a null dereference and fixing it would change results rather than prevent a fault: the interpreter returns 0 whenever the register's STATIC type is not HARRAY, whatever the value is, while the JIT reads the real size. So the two disagree for any program holding a live array in a register typed as something else. The interpreter is the oracle by convention, but this one should be settled against HashLink before either side moves -- and it wants its own change, with its own reasoning, not a rider on a crash fix.","files":null}]}